The '''Agostino high speed rail''' is a [[W:Transnational|transnational]] Balisca-Siculian high-speed [[AVB]] line, opened in 1980 between [[Alessandria station|Alessandria]] and [[Otranto station|Otranto]]. The Baliscan portion of the line was fully developed by [[Baliscan Railways Group|''Transmatarrañya'']], which is the main operator to this day. It is one of the oldest transnational [[w:High-speed rail|high-speed rail]] systems in the world and one of the most heavily used.

